cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FuelAnalyst, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "FuelAnalyst"
abstract: >-
  FuelAnalyst is an open-source Python package that calculates fuel loads and
  fire model inputs from forest fuel inventory data. From plot, tree,
  understory vegetation, canopy cover, and woody debris measurements, it
  estimates stand structure, tree biomass, canopy fuel attributes, and woody
  debris, shrub, herb, duff, and litter loads, and formats them as inputs to the
  Conifer Pyrometrics (ConPyro), Crown Fire Initiation and Spread (CFIS), and
  First Order Fire Effects (FOFEM) models.
